  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 250 AM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nThe CAMs model the upstream convection to top the stout upper ridge\nand then dive southward and eastward toward the PAH FA later \ntoday. There is variance amongst the HREF members on whether it \nwill hold together enough to impact us (HRRR/ARW) or not \n(NSSL/FV3). Their timing suggests by mid morning if it holds, \notherwise, its outflow boundary lay-out will allow for PM \ndevelopment along it. Either way, there is sufficient \ninstability to support our marginal risk of severe storms for \nmainly, damaging wind potential, which SPC pegs at 5%.\n\nAnother southward dive of energy is anticipated on Day-2\n(Monday), though the energy train displaces its axis further\neast with time. Once again, there is sufficient instability to\nsupport our marginal risk of severe storms for damaging wind\npotential, which again SPC pegs at 5%, over our northeast \ncounties.\n\nHeadline heat onsets today and continues thru Tuesday for\nanticipated heat indices up to around 112 degrees. We've \nupgraded our existing Advisory to a Warning, and expanded said \nAdvisory further to our east, \n\nWe'll return to more climatolically normal temperatures over \nthe back half of the week.",
